<article class="env-lemma" id="07J1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07J1">Lemma <span data-tag="07J1">60.12.5</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/07MF" data-tag="07MF">60.7.5</a>. Let $(U, T, \delta )$ be an object of $\text{Cris}(X/S)$. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (U(1), T(1), \delta (1)) = (U, T, \delta ) \times (U, T, \delta )  \]
</div>
  <p> in $\text{Cris}(X/S)$. Let $\mathcal{K} \subset \mathcal{O}_{T(1)}$ be the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals corresponding to the closed immersion $\Delta : T \to T(1)$. Then $\mathcal{K} \subset \mathcal{J}_{T(1)}$ is preserved by the divided structure on $\mathcal{J}_{T(1)}$ and we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\Omega _{X/S})_ T = \mathcal{K}/\mathcal{K}^{[2]}  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that $U = U(1)$ as $U \to X$ is an open immersion and as (<a href="/tag/07IH" data-tag="07IH">60.9.1.1</a>) commutes with products. Hence we see that $\mathcal{K} \subset \mathcal{J}_{T(1)}$. Given this fact the lemma follows by working affine locally on $T$ and using Lemmas <a href="/tag/07J0" data-tag="07J0">60.12.4</a> and <a href="/tag/07HV" data-tag="07HV">60.6.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>